<title>GERMANY: German insurer warns of huge EMU-related costs.</title>
<headline>German insurer warns of huge EMU-related costs.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>German insurers could face huge added costs because of the single European currency, one of the leading executives in the filed warned on Monday.</p>
<p>Speaking in Munich, Gerhard Rupprecht, chairman of life insurer Allianz Leben said that if, as the transition from marks to euros were made, new insurance contracts had to be expressed in both currencies, it could lead to &quot;enormous additional costs&quot; for insurers.</p>
<p>Rupprecht, according to the text of a speech published in advance, said clear guidelines for the conversion to the euro had quickly to be formulated.</p>
</text>
